# WRITTEN BEFORE ANY OTHER FILE IN THIS REPO, ON PURPOSE.
#
# The project charter rules that the portfolio version of this tracker carries synthetic
# or anonymized data only, and that the real ECCC export never leaves the working folder.
# A .gitignore added later is a .gitignore added after the first accidental commit.
#
# EVERY COMMENT IS ON ITS OWN LINE, AND THAT IS NOT A STYLE CHOICE.
# Git only treats # as a comment at the start of a line. An earlier version of this file
# wrote `store/    # the database file`, which git read as a pattern named
# "store/    # the database file" and matched nothing at all. The first `git status`
# listed store/ as ready to commit, which is how it was found. Do not put a comment after
# a pattern.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- real data, never commit

# The real weekly timeline export.
landing/

# The database file and the CSV backups taken after every approved import.
store/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

# The reverse of the anonymisation: these map an invented name back to a real person.
conf/name_map.local.json
*.real.bak

# Any workbook is assumed to be real until proven otherwise. The two exceptions are the
# data dictionary, which is the contract, and the invented sample workbooks.
*.xlsx
!conf/data_dictionary.xlsx
!sample_data/*.xlsx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- old manual backups

# Dated copies of the whole project folder, from before this was under version control.
# Committing them would put several copies of the project inside the repo.
snapshots/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ordinary noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
